<figure class="visual">
        <figcaption class="visual-cap"><span class="label">AWS load balancing · comparison matrix</span><h3>Which service makes which decision?</h3><p>Choose by traffic semantics, destination, address model, and scope. These services can be combined in one architecture.</p></figcaption>
        <div class="matrix-wrap">
          <table class="matrix">
            <caption>Capabilities and decision boundaries for ALB, NLB, GWLB, and standard AWS Global Accelerator.</caption>
            <thead><tr><th>Decision / option</th><th>ALB<br/><span class="read-chip">reads HTTP</span></th><th>NLB<br/><span class="read-chip">balances flows</span></th><th>GWLB<br/><span class="read-chip">inserts appliances</span></th><th>Global Accelerator<br/><span class="read-chip">selects regional entry</span></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Scope + role</th><td data-label="ALB">Regional application proxy · Layer 7</td><td data-label="NLB">Regional transport load balancer · Layer 4</td><td data-label="GWLB">Regional routed inspection path · Layer 3</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">Global standard accelerator · TCP/UDP delivery</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Accepted traffic</th><td data-label="ALB">HTTP, HTTPS<br/>WebSockets · HTTP/2 · gRPC support</td><td data-label="NLB">TCP, TLS, UDP, TCP_UDP, QUIC, TCP_QUIC<br/><span class="verified">verified 2026-09-10</span></td><td data-label="GWLB">IP packets; GENEVE encapsulation to appliances on UDP 6081</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">TCP and UDP listeners</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Decision inputs</th><td data-label="ALB">Host, path, headers, method, query string, source-IP CIDR</td><td data-label="NLB">Listener and flow; dual-stack rules can match source IP version</td><td data-label="GWLB">VPC route to GWLBE; flow stickiness selects appliance</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">Client location, endpoint health, regional traffic dials, endpoint weights</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Selection chain</th><td data-label="ALB">Listener rule → action → target group → target</td><td data-label="NLB">Listener action → optional weighted target group selection → flow target</td><td data-label="GWLB">GWLBE → GWLB → appliance → GWLB → GWLBE</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">Listener → regional endpoint group → endpoint</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Destination types</th><td data-label="ALB">Instance, IP, Lambda<br/>ECS registers instance or IP targets</td><td data-label="NLB">Instance, IP, ALB<br/>ALB target requires TCP setup</td><td data-label="GWLB">GENEVE-capable appliances registered as instance or IP targets</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">ALB, NLB, EC2, Elastic IP<br/>GWLB is not an endpoint</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">TLS handling</th><td data-label="ALB">HTTPS listener terminates TLS; backend may use HTTP or HTTPS</td><td data-label="NLB">TLS listener terminates; TCP listener can pass TLS through</td><td data-label="GWLB">Transparent insertion; decryption and inspection depend on appliance</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">Endpoint handles TLS; accelerator does not terminate application TLS</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Address model</th><td data-label="ALB">DNS endpoint with changing IPs; internet-facing or internal</td><td data-label="NLB">Static address per enabled AZ; optional EIPs for internet-facing IPv4 NLB</td><td data-label="GWLB">Private GWLB endpoint used as a route-table target</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">Static anycast addresses; regional endpoints can change behind them</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">WAF + security</th><td data-label="ALB">AWS WAF integration; ALB and target security groups</td><td data-label="NLB">No AWS WAF integration; security groups can apply to the NLB</td><td data-label="GWLB">Appliances provide firewall, IDS, or IPS functions</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">No WAF integration at GA; associate WAF with an ALB endpoint</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Choose when</th><td data-label="ALB">HTTP applications need content routing, authentication, or WAF</td><td data-label="NLB">Transport workloads need flow balancing, zonal static addresses, or TLS pass-through</td><td data-label="GWLB">Traffic must traverse a scalable appliance fleet</td><td data-label="Global Accelerator">Multi-Region applications need global static entry and health-based regional selection</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway"><strong>Common compositions:</strong> Global Accelerator → ALB or NLB · NLB → ALB where its documented constraints fit · routed workload traffic → GWLBE ⇄ GWLB ⇄ appliance fleet.</div>
      </figure>
